{"agent_id":"slA5","agent_seq":159,"timestamp":"2026-09-04T22:43:39.537184154Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"eb8ac346-e59f-410e-8a2c-19a07db394d7","comment_uuid":"5bcd52e8-3163-42d1-b4df-b4822a330267","author":"slA5","content":"Goal solve Erdos881 active; session19 parent17/active18 made verified progress on far-pin construction viability. New DiagonalPinCertificates.lean: HasShortDiagonalRepairs R k a b for1<=j<k; monotone inR. IsPinnedAt.eq_allCopies_of_shortDiagonalRepairs forces n=k*b+a from any successor pin once n>=N+a. Two distinct retained anchors give no_pin_of_two_shortDiagonalRepairs from N+maxanchors. Refactored SubtupleRepair to expose tuple_with_anchor_of_selectedRepair for one actual tuple; original successorBasis theorem statement preserved as wrapper. FrozenPrefixCertificates.lean proves prefix96 {0,2,3,6,13,20,25,49,50,51,73} has helpers49,50,51,73 NEVER pinned in any superset covering from3 atorder3. Explicit pairs/triples for anchors<=3; n<6 excluded byb<=n. These are only FOUR finite exceptions, not a general counterexample exclusion; repairs use otherhelpers, so no safe joint deletion. Corrected docs suggestion these helpers might all be pinned later. New scripts pin_certificates.py (find2anchors, emit actualtuples, independently verifycertificate), probe_coherent_pin_extension.py (freeze every yes/no belowcutoff, requiredoldpoints nonvacuous, newtargets>cutoff, identicalN, independentSAT verification; separateCERTIFIED_NO_PIN_EXTENSION/UNSAT/UNKNOWN), test_pin_certificates.py. Exact prefix48 {0,1,2,6,9,22,32,40}: eachhelper individually pinnable atscale192 (32@113;40@192), BOTH newpins UNSAT at96,144,192 with100000conflicts. Scale384 BOTH UNKNOWN after100000conflicts32.25s; process exited, no livejobs. Important additional finding: actual model32@113 yields shortcert for40 anchors1,57 excludingpinsfrom60; model40@192 yields certfor32 anchors9,22 excludingfrom25. Both fullSAT models saved in tests and reproducibleCLI; each has n