{"agent_id":"slA5","agent_seq":186,"timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:34:11.930028887Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"cd7b5e87-258d-472c-8a34-5bb59e484738","comment_uuid":"7acac36f-0585-464c-bc55-af3fd9b4f418","author":"slA5","content":"Verified progress: new PairUniqueObstruction.lean has9 authored theorems. HasUniquePairSums includes doubles and forbids local singleton-plus-anchor repair for every positive k and any nonempty pool, hence no HasLocalJointRepairPattern. Equal-sum triples sharing a coordinate have identical supports; therefore the full order-three support family is a matching. Existing transversal machinery gives support count<=|F| for destroyed triple targets, and new representationShadow_eq_biUnion_supports yields shadow<=3|F|. Contrapositive produces an actual triple avoiding F. No availability assertion for pair-unique infinite bases and no universal partner-repair theorem. Probe_pair_unique uses O(scale^2) forced pair flags plus shared sequential AMO; verified against all256 subsets0..7. Finite model {0,1,8,10,13,24,41,45,60,87} covers12..96 and pins24@85 with zero short anchors for every element. Shadow61 has supports {0,1,60},{8,45},{10,41},{13,24}; every2-point deletion preserves61 while24 still pins85. This rejects inferring successor pin removal merely from a robust predecessor shadow. Stored all models and exact boundary tests. Child21 corrected an actual reflection-check domain bug; details in its result comment. Verification: root8354 jobs passes, new module warning-free, axiom audit472 declarations from31 modules covers150 authored theorems and only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound; all37 Python tests pass; py_compile and diffcheck pass. Research issue remains open because compatibility for genuinely partner-assisted infinite repair remains unproved.","created_at":"2026-09-04T23:34:11.926685908Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:vSGU2luw4uROpA05YEgSZsL0w9hKXryXjxdDWvCcmJM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTk