{"agent_id":"slA5","agent_seq":249,"timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:58:08.780483273Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b3b91c39-e215-4f52-ae74-3ad0fcbff577","comment_uuid":"1ba3c3f0-5aad-4a40-bfdd-e793d60ca35f","author":"slA5","content":"The one-residue accumulation obstruction is now proved, including an attained maximal tail modulus dividing every other one. A stronger next question is uniform modular thickness of tail k-fold sumsets: for an order-k basis A, does there exist C such that for every modulus q>0 and cutoffN, q<=C*|k(A>=N) modq|? Candidate proof: if ratios q/|k-tail residues| are unbounded, padding by one late a0 injects each lower-arity residue set into the k-arity one. The same density induction should then work with a finite residue set Gamma and recurrence c_j(x)<=|F|c_(j-1)(x)+|Gamma|*(floor(x/q)+1), forcing kA densityzero. This is NOT yet formalized; test the multi-residue recurrence and exact padding injection first. It would constrain growing residue patterns, not automatically construct a successor deletion or classify mandatory anchors.","created_at":"2026-09-05T01:58:08.777238584Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:vSGU2luw4uROpA05YEgSZsL0w9hKXryXjxdDWvCcmJM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUTS0dMLYCeyVs6Rbonl0CdichTlwV6pfVQFnzhkLJ/cAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAc6cBt75wh78MDQzv04w2Yhg6nAH70GUjSNpXCkWa/1ZjfX8jZiFT4aMjkeWuBKJdcogQIZ2WZELUDzR0G+eMCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:vSGU2luw4uROpA05YEgSZsL0w9hKXryXjxdDWvCcmJM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgUTS0dMLYCeyVs6Rbonl0CdichTlwV6pfVQFnzhkLJ/cAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJXFzrO+CvlNjl43D9Oi5Ksmkd37ILHORdpqgzvfaHgE4kvWZNe/6rBI0Vu12xrrbto2tBtlyD9wsUv2eRHukgs="}
